{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1437161-the-realm-of-infusion","id":1437161,"title":"The REALM of Infusion","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-02-26T16:38:18-08:00","id":1437161,"title":"The REALM of Infusion","content":"I have been thinking again about the art of Infusion and how it doesn't quite match up to what it wants to do in c20. That it is a bit of a &quot;Meta art&quot; depending heavily on particular realms. But what if it were a Meta realm like Time of Scene. Something you add into a cantrip like to allow a variety of themes from the creation fo temporary items to treasurs to who unique art combos...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-27T14:58:35-08:00","id":1437286,"title":"","content":"This will probably not help at all, but frankly i just writte off both infusion and the art of making pacts and vows (forgot the name). To me they just sound tone deaf with the rest of the entire game. I rather leave things like vows and infusion as sort of roleplay aspect of the game, where the storyteller and players sort things in case by case. <br /> <br /> Both arts feel like trying to gamefy aspects of the game that had no need to be gamefied. Infusion less so than the vow art. But you will always reach a point where the art system is limiting the roleplay more than anything, and you enter a zone of &quot;only NPCs do that&quot;. or then you instead begin to make house rules to X or Y scenario, until you realize you should have been better off with no hard rules. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26021-rucun","name":"Rucun","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-28T03:42:24-08:00","id":1437338,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rucun</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1437161-the-realm-of-infusion?p=1437286#post1437286\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This will probably not help at all, but frankly i just writte off both infusion and the art of making pacts and vows (forgot the name). To me they just sound tone deaf with the rest of the entire game. I rather leave things like vows and infusion as sort of roleplay aspect of the game, where the storyteller and players sort things in case by case.<br /> <br /> Both arts feel like trying to gamefy aspects of the game that had no need to be gamefied. Infusion less so than the vow art. But you will always reach a point where the art system is limiting the roleplay more than anything, and you enter a zone of &quot;only NPCs do that&quot;. or then you instead begin to make house rules to X or Y scenario, until you realize you should have been better off with no hard rules.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Its good your game doesn't allow Boggans, Nockers, House Dougal or anyone who buys crafting. Seriously &quot;Fairies making magic stuff&quot; or tricksy contracts are pretty much core feats that should be there before anything else not a tone deaf attempt. Its like a vampire game without having Mind control. Or a werewolf game where you don't turn into a wolf.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-28T08:36:31-08:00","id":1437356,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1437161-the-realm-of-infusion?p=1437338#post1437338\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Its good your game doesn't allow Boggans, Nockers, House Dougal or anyone who buys crafting. Seriously &quot;Fairies making magic stuff&quot; or tricksy contracts are pretty much core feats that should be there before anything else not a tone deaf attempt. Its like a vampire game without having Mind control. Or a werewolf game where you don't turn into a wolf.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> That's exactly my point. Pacts should be a core feat to all changelings and all players, they shouldn't have to spend points in this art to have it.<br /> By making it a art you not only have to spend points for it, but sometimes even having the art is not enough, you need all 5 levels of it. <br /> I rather do it how the second edition, anyone can do vows, just sprinkle a point of glamour over it to make it official and make the dreaming enforce it.<br /> <br /> <br /> Your example should actually be &quot;What if there was a werewolf game where becoming crinos is a level 3 gift?&quot;<br /> <br /> Because that's what happens with vows. <br /> <br /> <br /> And Im not against changelings creating stuff, Im against they needing a art to do it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26021-rucun","name":"Rucun","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-28T22:02:03-08:00","id":1437421,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rucun</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1437161-the-realm-of-infusion?p=1437356#post1437356\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> That's exactly my point. Pacts should be a core feat to all changelings and all players, they shouldn't have to spend points in this art to have it.<br /> By making it a art you not only have to spend points for it, but sometimes even having the art is not enough, you need all 5 levels of it.<br /> I rather do it how the second edition, anyone can do vows, just sprinkle a point of glamour over it to make it official and make the dreaming enforce it.<br /> <br /> <br /> Your example should actually be &quot;What if there was a werewolf game where becoming crinos is a level 3 gift?&quot;<br /> <br /> Because that's what happens with vows.<br /> <br /> <br /> And Im not against changelings creating stuff, Im against they needing a art to do it.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You're wrong about two points?<br /> <br /> Changelings can make new oaths. There are rules on page 264. They couldn't make oaths with non changelings that were supernatural or punishable before. This Contracts lets you make superanturally binding Oaths with Mortals/vampires/etc. This is not a power they had before at all. It is close to a generic power the LOST have.<br /> <br /> Werewolf does include a number of &quot;Super form&quot; gifts so I honestly probably wouldn't mind a werewolf game where your base forms are Homid, Galabro and Wolf form. That would you know cover all the basics with a Room to grow for the focused murder machine.<br /> <br /> Infusion is not meant to take the place of crafting mechanical but allow greater focus. Anyone can learn to swing a sword but there's combat focused powers in all the games. No one begrudges the idea and says &quot;ALL VAMPIRES SHOULD JUST BE SUPER STRONG&quot; and bitch that potence exists.<br /> <br /> Neither Infusion as presented in the books nor Contracts is what you think it is. They are specializations. Infusion doesn't do a great job of this.. and its debateable how good a job Dragon ire is as a combat art but yeah that some changelings might be better at something because they spend xp seems pretty basic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-11T18:25:46-08:00","id":1439334,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1437161-the-realm-of-infusion?p=1437421#post1437421\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> You're wrong about two points?<br /> <br /> Changelings can make new oaths. There are rules on page 264. They couldn't make oaths with non changelings that were supernatural or punishable before. This Contracts lets you make superanturally binding Oaths with Mortals/vampires/etc. This is not a power they had before at all. It is close to a generic power the LOST have.<br /> <br /> Werewolf does include a number of &quot;Super form&quot; gifts so I honestly probably wouldn't mind a werewolf game where your base forms are Homid, Galabro and Wolf form. That would you know cover all the basics with a Room to grow for the focused murder machine.<br /> <br /> Infusion is not meant to take the place of crafting mechanical but allow greater focus. Anyone can learn to swing a sword but there's combat focused powers in all the games. No one begrudges the idea and says &quot;ALL VAMPIRES SHOULD JUST BE SUPER STRONG&quot; and bitch that potence exists.<br /> <br /> Neither Infusion as presented in the books nor Contracts is what you think it is. They are specializations. Infusion doesn't do a great job of this.. and its debateable how good a job Dragon ire is as a combat art but yeah that some changelings might be better at something because they spend xp seems pretty basic.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> My bad, I wasn't aware oaths remained and thought they &quot;gamefied it&quot; just like they turned dragon's ire into an art. Seens like I jumped to conclusions. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26021-rucun","name":"Rucun","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"113"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}